From f833d4562f2adda905042b2e8ea3b36d24bc5197 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: FiyeroT <me@fiyero.xyz>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 11:27:48 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 023/126] urltest: download 64 KiB through a member before
 switching to it

A server behind a DPI that freezes every connection after ~16 KB passes
the small URL test with a good delay, and the group selects a member
through which only small requests work.

Before the group switches to a member it now reads 64 KiB of the download
test URL through it. A member whose download began and stopped is passed
over until its next periodic result; a frozen member taken as the last
resort is tested again then. A test that could not run (a status, a TLS
error, a short body) holds no member back and is logged at warn. While a
selection waits for such tests, connections go by the plain choice, one
selection at most waits, and the Clash API does not wait for it.

The URL comes from SING_BOX_URLTEST_DOWNLOAD_URL (the package sets it
from /etc/config/sing-box); without it nothing changes.
